# Single-source normalize

When running or editing `scripts/normalize.mjs`:

- Default `pnpm normalize` uses `--source all` (Cursor + Grok/Kilo/Cline).
- Use `pnpm normalize:host` (`--source host`) when you only want Cursor host trees or to avoid scanning large agent harvests.
- Dedup always runs per `session_id` (prefers host, then grok, workspace-scoped paths, newer mtime).
- Prefer `host` over `all` on duplicated host+devcontainer trees if agents are not needed.

Subagent files must pass through `parent_session_id` on each turn when `raw_path` contains `/subagents/`.
